      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC", "unconnected-(C13-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "The two FCC1 VCAP pins are assigned to the UART3 connector nets, while C13.1, a 2u2 capacitor, is unconnected.",
      "expected": "VCAP pins should have the required local capacitors to ground and should not be used as UART signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"143\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"145\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"165\") (name \"unconnected-(C13-Pad1)\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The H753's internal regulator decoupling is not provided at its VCAP pins, and the UART3 connector is connected to those regulator pins instead of usable UART signals. This can prevent proper FCC operation and makes UART3 unusable.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present. The MCU VDD pins are unconnected, both external crystal circuits are misrouted, and the FCC VCAP pins are used as UART3 signals rather than being properly decoupled."
}

